Picking the Perfect Theme Colors

After finally getting rid of "footer test", I turned my attention to the typography and colors. A harsh, stark white background didn't feel right.

I asked the Google search AI:

> *"I'm styling my blog—pick a sophisticated color palette that feels like a classic newspaper."*

The AI assistant, overachiever that it is, started listing all kinds of design tips I hadn't even asked for, alongside 3 color recommendations. From those, I chose a warm, paper-like off-white for the background instead of blinding white, and a soft charcoal for the text instead of pitch black.

I dressed up my personal daily blog with these colors, and it looked gorgeous. Pure satisfaction.

However, when I tried to apply the exact same palette to my official Soosooland blog, Claude interrupted me. It reminded me that we had agreed to keep my two personas distinct, suggesting that the official project blog should stick to its own branding. So, I opted for a sleek chalkboard theme instead.

